# Day 55/60 — Continue Core Feature Development

## Objective

Continue implementing the capstone project's core functionality while maintaining stability, verifying previous features, and improving overall code quality.

---

## What Was Completed

- Continued development of core project features
- Integrated new functionality into the existing architecture
- Verified previously implemented features still worked correctly
- Debugged integration issues
- Refactored complex or duplicated code
- Updated project documentation
- Committed verified progress to GitHub

---

## What I Learned

### Stable Software Requires Continuous Verification

As new features are added, previously completed functionality should always be tested again.

### Refactoring Improves Long-Term Maintainability

Cleaning up code early prevents technical debt from growing as the project becomes more complex.

### Incremental Progress Reduces Risk

Building, testing, and verifying each milestone creates a far more reliable development workflow than implementing multiple features simultaneously.

